{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1429467-published-story-hooks-do-you-use-them-why-or-why-not","id":1429467,"title":"Published Story Hooks: Do you use them, why or why not?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-21T22:51:04-08:00","id":1429467,"title":"Published Story Hooks: Do you use them, why or why not?","content":"Hoping the subject was clear enough. But to explain, a lot of the books in Chronicles offer Story Hooks (in a sidebar, usually 3 of them) when introducing new concepts or creatures. They are common in Night Horrors books but have been seen elsewhere, for instance each Lodge in the Werewolf Lodge books has a sidebar with three, as does the Mage Legacy books, and many of the locations in the second edition core books.<br /> <br /> But I never hear people talk about them except as an explanation for their view on the lore.<br /> <br /> So, do you use them? What made you want to use them?<br /> <br /> If not, what keeps you from doing it? (Feel free to just say you don't like them, or need them, I want as many honest responses as possible).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-22-2020, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-25T22:19:44-08:00","id":1429920,"title":"","content":"I use them for inspiration. At the least they aren't tailored for my group and often seem written for the simplest mind in the gene pool, but even though I never use them as written many of my best ideas were at least sparked by one of these offerings, if not outright just being a heavily modified version of one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T05:37:51-08:00","id":1430218,"title":"","content":"I've made a lot of use from them. I see it pretty pragmatically: I paid for the book, so I want to use the material in there. Same goes for sample NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T08:06:06-08:00","id":1430234,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve never run CoD but if I ran a game I would definitely use at least some of the published story hooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T09:37:43-08:00","id":1430240,"title":"","content":"Games I've been in have involved the party discovering the in-world clanbook compilations and hunting a variant of Andrew the Tanner.<br /> <br /> The game didn't get <i>around</i> to using it much, but we were also very much planning on using the rumor hook in Night Horrors: Count ******* Dracula where he was suggested to be the Impaler's Promethean creation rather than grandchilde.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-28T12:26:45-08:00","id":1430251,"title":"","content":"I remember Andrew Tanner. From Shadows of the UK. Made my skin crawl.<br /> <br /> I wish they had done something with Southampton in that book. My friend lives there. It would\u2019ve been cool to show her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T13:51:40-08:00","id":1430606,"title":"","content":"I use them for inspiration, but I also think they're useful as clarification for how a given element would fit into a game. I sometimes finish a section of a book and find myself thinking, &quot;Okay, that's cool worldbuilding, but what am I supposed to do with it?&quot; So the hooks help contextualize and pull things together, even if I don't end up actually deploying them as written.<br /> <br /> I've been getting a lot of mileage out of the crossover stuff in Dark Eras 2 and Contagion Chronicle for this exact reason - I'm running a Demon game that also (so far) features hunters and a Promethean, so stuff like the Milton Keynes chapter of Contagion Chronicle has helped me work out how other splats relate to God-Machine nonsense and vice-versa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-31T23:25:39-08:00","id":1430650,"title":"","content":"I would love to see some more SAS style adventures published for CofD. Some of these books have such rich settings that I think it can be difficult for some groups to wrap their heads around the setting. Some new adventures for 2E would help with this so much. <br /> <br /> White Wolf greenlit Onyx Path to write adventures for Masquerade 5E, so maybe there is some hope?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1310-samare","name":"Samare","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1310_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-01-06T00:05:07-08:00","id":1431254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1429467-published-story-hooks-do-you-use-them-why-or-why-not?p=1430251#post1430251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember Andrew Tanner. From Shadows of the UK. Made my skin crawl.<br /> <br /> I wish they had done something with Southampton in that book. My friend lives there. It would\u2019ve been cool to show her.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoever Liked this post: Thank you \ud83d\ude0a\ud83d\ude0a\ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}